Package: TTPsplines
Title: Tensor-Train P-Splines for Multidimensional Smoothing and GLMs
Version: 0.0.0.9001
Authors@R: c(
    person("Dae-Jin", "Lee", , "dae-jin.lee@ie.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9090-0475")),
    person("Rafael", "Ballester-Ripoll", role = "ctb",
           comment = "planned collaborator")
  )
Description: Statistical Tensor-Train (TT) P-spline smoothing for non-additive
    multidimensional regression on scattered continuous covariates. The
    coefficient array Theta is stored and optimized in TT format with classical
    directional discrete-difference (P-spline) penalties. The package targets
    smoother practice -- Gaussian / Poisson / Bernoulli via ALS / PIRLS / L-BFGS,
    family-aware optimizer='auto', fixed or conditional GCV (cGCV) for anisotropic
    lambda, predictive rank helpers, and GLAM / full-tensor baselines when feasible
    -- rather than claiming priority for TT of B-spline coefficients with
    difference penalties (see related system-identification work). Development
    version; the public API may still change.
